# Centralized chart and component version pins.
# Source this file from scripts that need version info.

STRIMZI_VERSION="1.2.0"
STRIMZI_KAFKA_VERSION="1.2.0-kafka-4.3.1"
LITMUS_CHART_VERSION="3.28.0"
LITMUS_VERSION="3.28.0"
PROMETHEUS_STACK_VERSION="82.4.3"
KAFKA_IMAGE="quay.io/strimzi/kafka:${STRIMZI_KAFKA_VERSION}"
JAEGER_CHART_VERSION="3.4.1"
CERT_MANAGER_VERSION="v1.17.1"
BOOTSTRAP="krafter-kafka-bootstrap.kafka.svc:9092"

# Local-cluster toolchain.
#
# These were previously declared nowhere central: the kind binary was pinned in
# two workflows as duplicated `env:` blocks, the node image three times inside
# config/cluster.yaml, and a third figure — a floor, not a pin — in the
# installation guide. Nothing tied them together, and they had already drifted.
#
# config/cluster.yaml cannot read this file — kind takes a literal config with no
# variable substitution — so scripts/check-versions.sh asserts the two agree
# rather than generating one from the other.
#
# KINDEST_NODE_VERSION is v1.34.x rather than the newest kind publishes, and that
# is the choice, not an oversight: v1.34.11 is the OLDEST image v0.33.0 still
# ships prebuilt, so this is the largest jump in tooling for the smallest jump in
# Kubernetes. There is no v1.31 image for a current kind, so standing still was
# not on the menu.
KIND_VERSION="v0.33.0"
KINDEST_NODE_VERSION="v1.34.11"
# Same minor as the node image. It was two minors above it for a long time —
# outside the supported ±1 skew — which check-versions.sh now fails on.
KUBECTL_VERSION="v1.34.11"
